================================================================================
Foundation model
================================================================================

Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M — a geospatial foundation model developed by NASA and IBM,
released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  Paper: "Prithvi-EO-2.0: A Versatile Multi-Temporal Foundation Model for Earth
         Observation Applications", arXiv:2412.02732.

  This project uses the frozen Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M backbone and adds:
    - LoRA adapters (rank 16, alpha 32) on the q/k/v projections of the encoder,
    - a pre-projection LayerNorm + a linear 1024->32 projector, and
    - a Temporal Fusion Transformer (TFT) forecasting head.
  The base backbone weights are NOT modified (they are frozen). They are included,
  baked into the distributed model bundle, and are byte-identical to the base model;
  they are not redistributed as a separate artifact.

  The Prithvi architecture code (prithvi_mae.py) is redistributed under Apache-2.0.

