Datasets and services (used at training and/or inference time)
================================================================================

Each of the following carries its own terms of use. Users are responsible for
complying with the terms of any dataset or service they access.

  - MODIS MOD13Q1 (vegetation indices / NDVI) ....... NASA
  - Harmonized Landsat Sentinel-2 (HLS) imagery ..... NASA
  - SMAP (soil moisture) ............................ NASA
  - ERA5-Land (weather / land reanalysis) ........... ECMWF / Copernicus Climate
                                                      Change Service (C3S)
  - Land cover (ESA WorldCover v200) ............... ESA / Copernicus (CC BY 4.0)
  - Administrative boundaries ....................... CoreStack (core-stack.org)
  - Forecast weather ............................... Open-Meteo
  - Satellite / geospatial data access ............. Google Earth Engine

================================================================================
Optional local LLM (advisory phraser — not shipped, not redistributed)
================================================================================

The advisory layer can OPTIONALLY use a small local language model to reword the
rule engine's chosen message and (optionally) translate it. It is OFF by default
(ADVISORY_SLM=0 uses a deterministic template), and NO model weights are shipped
or redistributed with this project — the operator pulls them locally at their own
discretion. When enabled:

  - Gemma (e.g. gemma3) — Google. Use is governed by the Gemma Terms of Use
    (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms) and the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy.
  - Ollama (local model runtime) — MIT License.
